 "_doc": "Design 125 step 2 (§4a A3, A4), the Apple Wi-Fi lookup's shared contract, kept once in contracts/integrations/wifi_lookup/ (design 133). rules: the server's cache months (a positive row fresh fresh_months calendar months from the month Apple answered, a negative until the month it was asked in ends, UTC) and the phone's stale_grace_h. policy: the policy's wifi_lookup. request: the exact body of POST /api/devices/wifi-lookup. answers: each case the server's tests produce (only asked BSSIDs; fresh_months_left, never a month; off also while the phone's location is off). phone_answers: the phone's action for each status and body (use: the rows stored; wait_s: no ask for that long; off: none until a policy says on). phone_rows: what the phone keeps from a 200 at now, and until when (storeApple). Design 125b (cells): rules' cells_max, cells_a_day (the per-phone brake), cell_answer_after_s (a cells answer's fixed time through a proxy - the gate's 3 s, the Apple call's 10 s and a second; 9 s direct is the server's alone), cell_row_days and cell_negative_days (the phone's rows). request_cells: the exact cells body. cell_forms: a cell's wire form to valid or not (the server's cells::Cell::parse, the launcher's cellWire). cell_answers: each cells case the server's tests produce - no age, no cached mark, the same body from the cache as from Apple; each asked string echoed. cell_phone_answers: the phone's action for each (the cell wait alone; a 409 both waits). cell_phone_rows: what the phone keeps from a cells 200 at now, and until when (storeAppleCells). Test network 001-01 only, made-up coordinates. Design 137 (cell neighbours): rules near_max (the near entries of one answer), near_per_cell (a stored list) and near_asked (the count of full-id neighbours one call asks Apple for). Every cells 200 has near - per asked cell in the ask order, each stored list nearest first, an entry already given or an asked cell left out; each cell in the wire form; ch and pci only when Apple sent them; never ch or pci in cells.",
